  "description": "Conversion of an existing garage into a habitable space, erection of a single storey rear extension. Hip to gable roof extension with rear dormer and installation of 2nos front rooflights.. Change of use of the existing dwellinghouse (Use Class C3) into a large 9 bedroom 9 person HMO (Use Class Sui Generis) with the provision of refuse and cycle storage.",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed loft-level bedrooms, by reason of their restricted internal floor-to-ceiling clearance of 2.2 metres, would fail to provide a satisfactory standard of residential accommodation for future occupiers, resulting in an oppressive and substandard living environment with inadequate head height, daylight penetration, and ventilation contrary to Policy D6 of the London Plan (2021), Policy DM10 of the Core Strategy (2012) , Policy Guidance 25 of the Royal Borough of Kingston upon Thames Residential Design SPD (2013), and the Nationally Described Space Standards (2015).\r",
    "In the absence of a detailed Surface Water Drainage Strategy, the applicant has failed to demonstrate how surface water runoff from the increased impermeable footprint will be managed on-site in accordance with the sustainable drainage hierarchy, or to satisfy the Lead Local Flood Authority that surface water flows will not discharge into the foul sewer, thereby presenting an unacceptable risk of localized flooding contrary to Policy SI 13 of the London Plan (2021) , Policy DM4 of the Core Strategy (2012), and the National Planning Policy Framework."
  ],
